From: SpiNativeWorker <spi-native@localhost>
Date: Wed, 8 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gdma: per-direction RST disarm for peripheral-handshake channels

Additive increment on top of the 0e2ab32b overlay restack; frozen inputs
are NOT rewritten.

First full-duplex loopback execution strict-paused at transfer start:
"SPI2 strict dependency: RX GDMA unavailable/short/owner or address
error" with the IN channel parked and zero error/DONE raw bits. Trace
evidence (temporary instrumented diagnostic build, reverted):

  GDMA_ARM chan=0 dir=IN  restart=0     <- driver arms RX inlink
  GDMA_PARK st=IN  fsm=1->0             <- driver's TX-channel reset
  GDMA_ARM chan=0 dir=OUT restart=0     <- driver arms TX outlink
  rx_channel resolution = UINT32_MAX    <- strict pause at USR

Root cause: the ordinary IDF6.1 SPI driver sets up a full-duplex DMA
transaction as gdma_reset(rx); arm(rx); gdma_reset(tx); arm(tx) on the
SAME GDMA channel (ESP32-S3 channels are duplex pairs; SPI_DMA_CH_AUTO
allocates one channel for both directions). The model performed a
channel-wide disarm (both directions parked, cursors cleared) on either
direction's CONF0.RST 1->0 edge, so the TX reset disarmed the just-armed
RX inlink.

TRM 3.6.2 gives each direction its own RST: GDMA_IN_RST_CHn resets the
RX FSM and RX FIFO pointer, GDMA_OUT_RST_CHn the TX side. The
channel-wide disarm (and quantum-BH cancel) remains for a coupled
memory-to-memory pair (MEM_TRANS_EN), whose transfer spans both
directions; peripheral-handshake chains are driven by peripheral
read/write calls, not the quantum BH.

Why connected passed but loopback failed: the connected NOR read has no
TX buffer, so no TX reset ever follows the RX arm; the loopback
full-duplex transaction has both send and receive buffers, hitting the
reset-after-arm ordering.

No interrupt semantics, descriptor cursor, EOF or 0001/0004 finish-path
behavior change; esp32c3 shares the same generic engine and TRM-faithful
semantics.
---
 hw/dma/esp_gdma.c | 20 +++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hw/dma/esp_gdma.c b/hw/dma/esp_gdma.c
--- a/hw/dma/esp_gdma.c
+++ b/hw/dma/esp_gdma.c
@@ -810,7 +810,25 @@ static void esp_gdma_write_chan_conf(ESPGdmaState *state, uint32_t dir,
             if (FIELD_EX32(value,  GDMA_IN_CONF0, RST) == 0 &&
                 FIELD_EX32(s->conf0, GDMA_IN_CONF0, RST) != 0)
             {
-                esp_gdma_channel_disarm(state, chan);
+                /* TRM 3.6.2: each direction's RST resets only its own FSM and
+                 * FIFO pointer; GDMA_OUT_RST_CHn must not disarm the IN side
+                 * of a peripheral-handshake channel (the ordinary SPI driver
+                 * resets RX then TX of the same channel while setting up a
+                 * full-duplex transaction). The channel-wide disarm remains
+                 * for a coupled memory-to-memory pair, whose quantum-driven
+                 * transfer spans both directions. */
+                if (FIELD_EX32(state->ch_conf[ESP_GDMA_IN_IDX][chan].conf0,
+                               GDMA_IN_CONF0, MEM_TRANS_EN)) {
+                    esp_gdma_channel_disarm(state, chan);
+                } else {
+                    esp_gdma_park(s);
+                    s->pending_start = false;
+                    s->pending_restart = false;
+                    s->rx_last_desc_addr = 0;
+                    s->rx_last_prev_addr = 0;
+                    s->rx_packet_ended = false;
+                }
                 esp_gdma_fsm_reset(s);
             }
